00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:06.230 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  many recipes call for shredded  ingredients which is why a cheese grater  is an indispensable kitchen tool  depending on which type of blade or  blades a grater has you can coarsely  shred to finely grate not just cheese  but also potatoes and vegetables  [Music]  graters come in different sizes shapes  and configurations  from flat models with one blade  to box graters with a different blade on  each side  the blades are made from a stainless  steel sheet that's just 1 50th of an  inch thick  the sheet enters a shearing machine  where a dye descends and cuts the blade  shape holes and all  [Music]  the machine's dies are interchangeable  so when it's time to produce a different  model workers simply remove this die and  install another one  stainless steel is the ideal blade  material because it's food safe durable  and rust proof  for this model the next step is to curve  the blade  they insert it into a press that bends  it with a rounded die  the press also turns over the edges  along three sides forming a channel for  a handle  the handle is made of stainless steel  wire  [Music]  a bending machine wraps it around a  grader shaped form  then cuts the end free releasing what is  now a finished handle  [Music]  [Music]  now for this model's final assembly  workers slide a handle into the blade's  channels  [Music]  next they put the blade in a press which  forces the channels closed encasing the  wire  with the handle and blade now locked  together the grater is finished  [Music]  another model has a built-in tray to  collect the grated food  this machine forms the pivoting handle  which enables the blade to stand upright  in the tray  first the machine cuts a strip of  stainless steel to the required length  it makes holes for a rivet on each side  then it bends the piece to a u-shape  [Music]  meanwhile a forming press shapes the  tray out of a stainless steel sheet  [Music]  the tray moves to the next press which  slices off the excess from the perimeter  [Music]  [Music]  the tray is now completely formed  all that's left to do is punch a hole on  each side for the rivets that attach the  handle that props up the blade  they take the handle and rivet it to one  end of the blade  [Music]  next they rivet the tray to the other  end of the blade  and the grater is fully assembled  [Music]  this company packages certain models in  blister packs  workers put the grater in a clear  plastic cover  then position a printed cardboard  backing over it  the backing is coated with transparent  heat activated glue  a few seconds under a hot press  and the plastic cover adheres to the  backing encapsulating the grater  from a basic version on up a grader is  an essential kitchen tool most cooks  can't do without  [Music]  you

